/-! Data of the bitset certificate for the Sixth binary forest.

The twenty roots are one point of each orbit of the group generated by the fifteen Sixth spatial
generators on the singular binary masks: zero, nine short classes and ten type-four classes.
The 33 doubling steps are words in the fifteen generators together with row operations
computing the binary matrix of each word. All data are discovery outputs; the kernel checks every
use, through the generic bitset operations `tenthForestDouble` and `tenthForestOpsMap`. -/

@[expose] public section
namespace FormalizedTextbooks.FrenkelLepowskyMeurmanMonster

